<title>USA: Maine needs more funds to buy Sears Island.</title>
<headline>Maine needs more funds to buy Sears Island.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maine's Department of Transportation might need more money to pull off a plan to buy Sears Island for $4.5 million.</p>
<p>But conservation groups, which are working to preserve the 940-acre island, hope to bid for it. Conservationists say a proposal to turn the island into a wildlife refuge with a visitors center has attracted strong public and private interest.</p>
<p>More than 15 years and $20 million have been spent so far to try to develop a deep water cargo port.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
